{
  "name": "SYS Error Handler",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "491289131665",
      "name": "Error Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.errorTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// n8n's error payload varies by failure mode; normalise it once here.\nconst e = $input.first().json;\nconst wf = e.workflow || {};\nconst ex = e.execution || {};\nreturn [{ json: {\n  workflowName: wf.name || 'unknown',\n  executionId:  ex.id || '',\n  nodeName:     ex.lastNodeExecuted || '',\n  message:      (ex.error && ex.error.message) || e.message || 'unknown error',\n  // Credit exhaustion on AI nodes returns a failure result rather than a normal\n  // error. Retrying it just spends more, so flag it as its own condition.\n  isBilling: /credit|quota|billing|insufficient/i.test(\n               (ex.error && ex.error.message) || ''),\n}}];"
      },
      "id": "715542517161",
      "name": "Extract failure",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        220,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.TWENTY_BASE_URL }}/rest/automationRuns",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": false
            }
          }
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({\"workflowName\": $json.workflowName, \"status\": \"FAILED\", \"errorMessage\": $json.message, \"n8nExecutionId\": $json.executionId, \"startedAt\": $now.toUTC().toISO() }) }}"
      },
      "id": "239445548592",
      "name": "Log failure",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4,
      "position": [
        560,
        300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "name": "Twenty API"
        }
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 5,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "={{ $env.TWENTY_BASE_URL }}/rest/automationRuns?filter=workflowName[eq]:{{ encodeURIComponent($json.workflowName) }},status[eq]:FAILED&order_by=startedAt[DescNullsLast]&limit=5",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": false
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "893486661029",
      "name": "Recent failures?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4,
      "position": [
        1120,
        300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "name": "Twenty API"
        }
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 5,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One failing workflow can fire hundreds of times. Alert on the first, then\n// stay quiet for an hour \u2014 an alert nobody can act on trains people to ignore\n// the channel, which is worse than no alert at all.\nconst runs = ($input.first().json.data?.automationRuns) || [];\nconst hourAgo = Date.now() - 3600_000;\nconst priors = runs.filter(r => new Date(r.startedAt).getTime() > hourAgo).length;\nreturn [{ json: { ...$('Extract failure').first().json, suppress: priors > 1 } }];"
      },
      "id": "689347577629",
      "name": "Suppress alert storm",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1340,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.suppress }}",
              "rightValue": "false",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "866606309329",
      "name": "Should alert?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1560,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({\"channel\": \"#crm-alerts\", \"text\": `:rotating_light: *${$json.workflowName}* failed\nNode: \\`${$json.nodeName}\\`\nError: ${$json.message}\n${$json.isBilling ? ':credit_card: *Looks like an AI credit/billing failure \u2014 retrying will not help.*' : ''}\nExecution: ${$json.executionId}` }) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "403076751231",
      "name": "Alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4,
      "position": [
        1780,
        300
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 2000,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "731706150075",
      "name": "Suppressed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2000,
        490
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## When any automation fails\nEvery other workflow points its failures here, so there is one\nplace that knows something went wrong. Without it a workflow\ncan fail quietly for weeks and the first anyone hears is a\ncustomer asking why nobody replied.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "702810777662",
      "name": "1. When any automation fails",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Write it down in the CRM\nThe failure becomes a record in Twenty \u2014 which workflow, when,\nand the error. It lives with the business data rather than in a\nlog file nobody opens, so failures can be reported on like\nanything else.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "012521374989",
      "name": "2. Write it down in the CRM",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        540,
        80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Alert, but do not spam\nIf the same workflow already failed several times in the last\nhour, log it but stay quiet. One broken integration can\notherwise produce hundreds of messages overnight, and the team\nlearns to ignore the channel \u2014 worse than no alerting at all.",
        "height": 510,
        "width": 1080,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "676425611839",
      "name": "3. Alert, but do not spam",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1100,
        140
      ]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
